Z||000000||Matthew_Fiero||10-01-2001||05:26 PM||||Tonight i will be ordering the parts i need for my 85 Fiero GT 4spd<BR>i will be ordering a new master and slave cylinder for the clutch and new brake lines. When ordering the slave, does it come with the line that usually gets bent, or do i order that seperately? If it is seperate what is the exact name for that part.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Voytek||10-01-2001||05:46 PM||||The slave doesn't come with any lines - that's ordered separately.<P>Are you ordering the front-to-back clutch line?  They're a B*TCH to bend and install (I broke one).  You're better off installing a flexible steel braided line.  That's what I have and installation was a breeze.<P>I had it custom made at a Big Rig shop - those guys have all the means.  If you have the old line, just cut off the ends / fittings and ask them to incorporate them into the steel braided line.  Make sure it's really close with the diameter (doesn't have to be 100% same size).<P>The dealership wanted $220 CDN for a replacement line.  I had this one custom made for $80.  It took the guy 1 hour to make.  Good luck.<P><BR>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Voytek (edited 10-01-2001).]||||reg||1
